  "static_review_focus": [
    "Owning CFG merge must retain exact actual parameter origins and path-local transfer/liveness; same ClosureId is insufficient.",
    "Drop can settle responsibility on a path without invocation, but cannot fabricate call/give trace effects. Early Drop followed by a Take/Call on the same path must reject.",
    "Whole graph reachability, unique block/SSA identity, no backedge and prepaid work/capacity must be reconstructed independently. Path splitting must not introduce unbounded exponential proof enumeration.",
    "CT graph equality is only one layer: schema interning also preserves declaration/ordinal SourceLifeBinding. Relocation cannot bypass that private source binding or erase full actual vectors.",
    "Different source life declarations/ordinals remain distinct even when runtime callers pass the same concrete address; unused bad generic declarations cannot be validated by a coincident concrete instance.",
    "Closed Type-result First/Second controls are existing nominal-identity regressions, not a new G4.4.5 capability."
  ],
